      "text": {
        "title": "Der Morgen",
        "de": "Der Patient steht um sieben Uhr auf. Er nimmt die Tablette ein. Die Tochter ruft die Station an. Sie holt ihn heute ab. Die Pflegekraft kommt mit. Herr Yilmaz steht nicht früh auf.",
        "en": "The patient gets up at seven. He takes the tablet. His daughter calls the ward. She picks him up today. The nurse comes along. Mr Yilmaz does not get up early."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dialogue",
      "type": "dialogue",
      "label": "Dialogue",
      "title": "Morning on the ward",
      "instructions": "Find the prefix at the end of each sentence.",
      "scene": "7:05. Anna wakes Herr Yilmaz. His daughter will call.",
      "sceneTitle": "Aufstehen",
      "speakers": {
        "N": {
          "name": "Anna",
          "role": "Pflegekraft",
          "avatar": "🧑‍⚕️"
        },
        "P": {
          "name": "Herr Yilmaz",
          "role": "Patient",
          "avatar": "🧑🏽"
        }
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Guten Morgen. Stehen Sie bitte auf.",
          "en": "Good morning. Please get up."
        },
        {
          "who": "P",
          "de": "Ich stehe auf. Nehme ich die Tablette ein?",
          "en": "I am getting up. Do I take the tablet?"
        },
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Ja. Sie nehmen die Tablette ein. Ihre Tochter ruft die Station an.",
          "en": "Yes. You take the tablet. Your daughter is calling the ward."
        },
        {
          "who": "P",
          "de": "Holt sie mich heute ab?",
          "en": "Is she picking me up today?"
        },
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Ja, sie holt Sie ab. Ich komme mit.",
          "en": "Yes, she is picking you up. I am coming along."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "Prefix at the end",
      "story": [
        "The prefix is part of the verb, but in a main clause it leaves the verb and sits at the end. That is the sentence bracket.",
        "Infinitive and the Sie-imperative keep the prefix attached: <b>aufstehen</b>, <b>Stehen Sie auf</b> still splits, while the infinitive <b>einnehmen</b> is one word."
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Where is the prefix?",
          "columns": [
            "Form",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
